From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:22:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(editor): flag read-only files and confirm before saving
 them

Saving writes a temp file and renames it over the target, which succeeds
for a chmod 444 file whenever its directory is writable, so read-only
files were silently overwritten.

Record whether the file on disk has no write bits when it is loaded or
saved, show "(readonly)" on its tab, and ask "Cancel / Overwrite" before
File > Save writes it. LSP rename's save-on-rename skips such files and
leaves them dirty instead of overwriting them without asking.

Closes #277
